      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A diesel turbocharger uses exhaust gases to spin a turbine, which is connected by a shaft to a compressor. As the turbine spins rapidly, the compressor draws in ambient air and forces it into the engine's cylinders at a much higher pressure—this is the \"boost.\" Compressing the air increases its density, allowing the engine to burn more fuel and generate significantly more power.",
