      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That intense, screaming whistle is usually due to the very rapid passage of compressed, high-velocity air rushing through the intake piping and the compressor itself. The pitch is directly related to the speed of rotation and the tightness of the air path; higher boost equals faster spin and a higher pitch. Mechanically, it's just air moving extremely fast, but the human auditory system interprets those high frequencies as a more organic, intense sound.",
